{
  "_comment": [
    "Kates Resilience Test Examples",
    "POST http://localhost:8080/api/resilience",
    "",
    "Each entry is a ResilienceTestRequest combining:",
    "  - testRequest : performance benchmark, the body of POST /api/tests (load / stress / endurance)",
    "  - chaosSpec   : fault injection (DisruptionType + FaultSpec parameters)",
    "  - steadyStateSec    : warmup window before chaos is injected",
    "  - maxRecoveryWaitSec: max time to wait for cluster to return to steady state",
    "  - probes      : assertions evaluated at baseline, during chaos, and post-recovery",
    "",
    "Keys that start with _ are notes for the reader, and the Kates API ignores them.",
    "It ignores any other field it doesn't have too, so a misspelled field runs on its default.",
    "ResilienceTutorialTest (kates/src/test) fails on such a field, and on an example the API would refuse.",
    "A LOAD or ENDURANCE run starts one producer and one consumer; only STRESS and CAPACITY read numProducers.",
    "",
    "All examples target the 'krafter' cluster in namespace 'kafka'.",
    "Forward the Kates API to http://localhost:8080 and export KATES_API_KEY first: see _usage."
  ],

  "examples": [

    {
      "_name": "01 — Broker Crash (POD_KILL)",
      "_description": "Kill a random broker pod without SIGTERM. Validates ISR recovery and zero message loss with acks=all.",
      "_hypothesis": "Killing one broker triggers leader re-election within 10s. ISR expands back to 3/3 within 120s. Producer sees latency spike but 0 errors.",
      "testRequest": {
        "type": "LOAD",
        "spec": {
          "topic": "kates-events",
          "numRecords": 500000,
          "recordSize": 1024,
          "throughput": 5000,
          "acks": "all",
          "lingerMs": 5,
          "compressionType": "lz4",
          "enableIdempotence": true
        }
      },
      "chaosSpec": {
        "experimentName": "broker-crash",
        "disruptionType": "POD_KILL",
        "targetNamespace": "kafka",
        "targetLabel": "strimzi.io/pool-name=brokers-alpha",
        "chaosDurationSec": 30,
        "delayBeforeSec": 0
      },
      "steadyStateSec": 30,
      "maxRecoveryWaitSec": 120,
      "probes": [
        {
          "name": "isr-health-check",
          "type": "cmdProbe",
          "mode": "Continuous",
          "command": "kafka-topics.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --describe --under-replicated-partitions 2>/dev/null | grep -c 'Topic:' || echo '0'",
          "expectedOutput": "50",
          "comparator": "<=",
          "intervalSec": 10,
          "timeoutSec": 30
        },
        {
          "name": "cluster-ready",
          "type": "k8sProbe",
          "mode": "Edge",
          "command": "kafka Ready",
          "expectedOutput": "Ready",
          "comparator": "contains",
          "intervalSec": 15,
          "timeoutSec": 30
        }
      ]
    },

    {
      "_name": "02 — Graceful Broker Shutdown (POD_DELETE)",
      "_description": "Delete a broker pod with SIGTERM. Kafka controlled-shutdown transfers leadership before pod exits. Expects zero producer errors.",
      "_hypothesis": "Graceful shutdown gives Kafka time to transfer partition leadership. Producer should see <5s latency spike and 0 errors.",
      "testRequest": {
        "type": "LOAD",
        "spec": {
          "topic": "kates-results",
          "numRecords": 600000,
          "recordSize": 1024,
          "throughput": 2000,
          "acks": "all",
          "enableIdempotence": true
        }
      },
      "chaosSpec": {
        "experimentName": "graceful-broker-delete",
        "disruptionType": "POD_DELETE",
        "targetNamespace": "kafka",
        "targetLabel": "strimzi.io/pool-name=brokers-alpha",
        "chaosDurationSec": 60,
        "delayBeforeSec": 0,
        "gracePeriodSec": 30
      },
      "steadyStateSec": 30,
      "maxRecoveryWaitSec": 120,
      "probes": [
        {
          "name": "isr-health-check",
          "type": "cmdProbe",
          "mode": "Continuous",
          "command": "kafka-topics.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --describe --under-replicated-partitions 2>/dev/null | grep -c 'Topic:' || echo '0'",
          "expectedOutput": "0",
          "comparator": "<=",
          "intervalSec": 10,
          "timeoutSec": 30
        },
        {
          "name": "cluster-ready",
          "type": "k8sProbe",
          "mode": "Edge",
          "command": "kafka Ready",
          "expectedOutput": "Ready",
          "comparator": "contains",
          "intervalSec": 15,
          "timeoutSec": 30
        }
      ]
    },

    {
      "_name": "03 — CPU Exhaustion (CPU_STRESS)",
      "_description": "Exhaust 1 CPU core on the gamma broker while a producer writes 8 KB records at 1000 rec/s. Observes ISR shrink/expand cycle.",
      "_hypothesis": "CPU-starved follower falls behind replication. If lag > replica.lag.time.max.ms (30s), it is evicted from ISR. ISR recovers fully within 90s of chaos ending.",
      "testRequest": {
        "type": "LOAD",
        "spec": {
          "topic": "kates-results",
          "numRecords": 300000,
          "recordSize": 8192,
          "throughput": 1000,
          "acks": "all",
          "compressionType": "snappy",
          "enableIdempotence": true
        }
      },
      "chaosSpec": {
        "experimentName": "cpu-exhaustion",
        "disruptionType": "CPU_STRESS",
        "targetNamespace": "kafka",
        "targetLabel": "strimzi.io/pool-name=brokers-gamma",
        "chaosDurationSec": 120,
        "delayBeforeSec": 0,
        "cpuCores": 1
      },
      "steadyStateSec": 20,
      "maxRecoveryWaitSec": 90,
      "probes": [
        {
          "name": "isr-health-check",
          "type": "cmdProbe",
          "mode": "Continuous",
          "command": "kafka-topics.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --describe --under-replicated-partitions 2>/dev/null | grep -c 'Topic:' || echo '0'",
          "expectedOutput": "50",
          "comparator": "<=",
          "intervalSec": 10,
          "timeoutSec": 30
        },
        {
          "name": "producer-throughput",
          "type": "cmdProbe",
          "mode": "Continuous",
          "command": "kafka-producer-perf-test.sh --topic kates-probe-topic --num-records 10 --record-size 100 --throughput -1 --producer-props bootstrap.servers=localhost:9092 2>/dev/null | tail -1 | awk '{print $6}'",
          "expectedOutput": "0",
          "comparator": ">",
          "intervalSec": 15,
          "timeoutSec": 30
        }
      ]
    },

    {
      "_name": "04 — Memory Pressure (MEMORY_STRESS)",
      "_description": "Consume 500 MB on a broker pod to simulate a GC-heavy workload or memory leak, while three STRESS producers write 5000 rec/s each. Validates that the JVM does not OOM-kill the broker.",
      "_hypothesis": "Memory pressure forces more GC cycles and slows request handling. Producer p99 latency rises but the broker does not crash. ISR stays intact.",
      "testRequest": {
        "type": "STRESS",
        "spec": {
          "topic": "kates-events",
          "numRecords": 1000000,
          "recordSize": 1024,
          "throughput": 5000,
          "numProducers": 3,
          "acks": "all",
          "enableIdempotence": true
        }
      },
      "chaosSpec": {
        "experimentName": "memory-pressure",
        "disruptionType": "MEMORY_STRESS",
        "targetNamespace": "kafka",
        "targetLabel": "strimzi.io/pool-name=brokers-sigma",
        "chaosDurationSec": 60,
        "delayBeforeSec": 0,
        "memoryMb": 500
      },
      "steadyStateSec": 30,
      "maxRecoveryWaitSec": 90,
      "probes": [
        {
          "name": "producer-throughput",
          "type": "cmdProbe",
          "mode": "Continuous",
          "command": "kafka-producer-perf-test.sh --topic kates-probe-topic --num-records 10 --record-size 100 --throughput -1 --producer-props bootstrap.servers=localhost:9092 2>/dev/null | tail -1 | awk '{print $6}'",
          "expectedOutput": "0",
          "comparator": ">",
          "intervalSec": 15,
          "timeoutSec": 30
        },
        {
          "name": "cluster-ready",
          "type": "k8sProbe",
          "mode": "Edge",
          "command": "kafka Ready",
          "expectedOutput": "Ready",
          "comparator": "contains",
          "intervalSec": 15,
          "timeoutSec": 30
        }
      ]
    },

    {
      "_name": "05 — Disk Saturation (IO_STRESS)",
      "_description": "Inject disk I/O pressure (80% FS utilization) on the alpha broker while large uncompressed records are written. Validates log flush latency handling.",
      "_hypothesis": "Disk saturation delays log segment flushes. Broker falls behind replication, ISR shrinks, leader migrates. Producers stall during re-election. No data loss.",
      "testRequest": {
        "type": "LOAD",
        "spec": {
          "topic": "kates-audit",
          "numRecords": 200000,
          "recordSize": 16384,
          "throughput": 500,
          "acks": "all",
          "compressionType": "none",
          "enableIdempotence": true
        }
      },
      "chaosSpec": {
        "experimentName": "disk-saturation",
        "disruptionType": "IO_STRESS",
        "targetNamespace": "kafka",
        "targetLabel": "strimzi.io/pool-name=brokers-alpha",
        "chaosDurationSec": 90,
        "delayBeforeSec": 0,
        "fillPercentage": 80,
        "ioWorkers": 2
      },
      "steadyStateSec": 20,
      "maxRecoveryWaitSec": 120,
      "probes": [
        {
          "name": "isr-health-check",
          "type": "cmdProbe",
          "mode": "Continuous",
          "command": "kafka-topics.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --describe --under-replicated-partitions 2>/dev/null | grep -c 'Topic:' || echo '0'",
          "expectedOutput": "50",
          "comparator": "<=",
          "intervalSec": 10,
          "timeoutSec": 30
        },
        {
          "name": "producer-throughput",
          "type": "cmdProbe",
          "mode": "Continuous",
          "command": "kafka-producer-perf-test.sh --topic kates-probe-topic --num-records 10 --record-size 100 --throughput -1 --producer-props bootstrap.servers=localhost:9092 2>/dev/null | tail -1 | awk '{print $6}'",
          "expectedOutput": "0",
          "comparator": ">",
          "intervalSec": 15,
          "timeoutSec": 30
        }
      ]
    },

    {
      "_name": "06 — DNS Failure (DNS_ERROR)",
      "_description": "Inject DNS resolution failures on a broker pod. Validates that broker-to-broker and client-to-broker connections survive transient DNS outages.",
      "_hypothesis": "Kafka connections use cached DNS results. Short DNS outages (<30s) should not disconnect established broker connections. Consumer group coordinators may reassign.",
      "testRequest": {
        "type": "LOAD",
        "spec": {
          "topic": "kates-events",
          "numRecords": 400000,
          "recordSize": 512,
          "throughput": 3000,
          "consumerGroup": "dns-failure-cg",
          "acks": "all",
          "enableIdempotence": true
        }
      },
      "chaosSpec": {
        "experimentName": "dns-failure",
        "disruptionType": "DNS_ERROR",
        "targetNamespace": "kafka",
        "targetLabel": "strimzi.io/cluster=krafter,strimzi.io/broker-role=true",
        "chaosDurationSec": 30,
        "delayBeforeSec": 0
      },
      "steadyStateSec": 30,
      "maxRecoveryWaitSec": 90,
      "probes": [
        {
          "name": "cluster-ready",
          "type": "k8sProbe",
          "mode": "Edge",
          "command": "kafka Ready",
          "expectedOutput": "Ready",
          "comparator": "contains",
          "intervalSec": 15,
          "timeoutSec": 30
        },
        {
          "name": "consumer-latency",
          "type": "cmdProbe",
          "mode": "Continuous",
          "command": "kafka-consumer-groups.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --describe --group dns-failure-cg 2>/dev/null | awk 'NR>1{sum+=$6} END{print sum+0}'",
          "expectedOutput": "100000",
          "comparator": "<",
          "intervalSec": 15,
          "timeoutSec": 30
        }
      ]
    },

    {
      "_name": "07 — Network Partition (NETWORK_PARTITION)",
      "_description": "Isolate the sigma broker from the network. Validates that partition leaders migrate to alpha/gamma and consumer groups rebalance without losing messages.",
      "_hypothesis": "Network partition fences the sigma broker. Leader elections complete within 30s. Consumer group rebalances within 60s. Producers recover with 0 errors.",
      "testRequest": {
        "type": "LOAD",
        "spec": {
          "topic": "kates-events",
          "numRecords": 400000,
          "recordSize": 512,
          "throughput": 3000,
          "consumerGroup": "net-split-cg",
          "acks": "all",
          "enableIdempotence": true
        }
      },
      "chaosSpec": {
        "experimentName": "network-split",
        "disruptionType": "NETWORK_PARTITION",
        "targetNamespace": "kafka",
        "targetLabel": "strimzi.io/pool-name=brokers-sigma",
        "chaosDurationSec": 60,
        "delayBeforeSec": 0
      },
      "steadyStateSec": 15,
      "maxRecoveryWaitSec": 120,
      "probes": [
        {
          "name": "min-isr-check",
          "type": "cmdProbe",
          "mode": "Edge",
          "command": "kafka-topics.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --describe --unavailable-partitions 2>/dev/null | grep -c 'Topic:' || echo '0'",
          "expectedOutput": "5",
          "comparator": "<=",
          "intervalSec": 15,
          "timeoutSec": 30
        },
        {
          "name": "consumer-latency",
          "type": "cmdProbe",
          "mode": "Continuous",
          "command": "kafka-consumer-groups.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --describe --group net-split-cg 2>/dev/null | awk 'NR>1{sum+=$6} END{print sum+0}'",
          "expectedOutput": "100000",
          "comparator": "<",
          "intervalSec": 15,
          "timeoutSec": 30
        }
      ]
    },

    {
      "_name": "08 — Node Drain (NODE_DRAIN)",
      "_description": "Drain gamma, the Kubernetes node hosting the gamma broker pod, during a 5-minute ENDURANCE run. Validates that the Strimzi Drain Cleaner transfers leadership before eviction and the pod reschedules cleanly.",
      "_hypothesis": "Drain Cleaner intercepts the eviction, triggers Kafka controlled shutdown, and transfers all partition leaders off the node before the pod is evicted. Zero downtime expected.",
      "_note": "Kates sets no TARGET_NODE for Litmus node-drain, so envOverrides names the node: gamma, which runs brokers-gamma on the Kind lab (config/cluster.yaml). On another cluster, name the node that runs it.",
      "testRequest": {
        "type": "ENDURANCE",
        "spec": {
          "topic": "kates-results",
          "numRecords": 1000000,
          "recordSize": 1024,
          "throughput": 3000,
          "durationMs": 300000,
          "consumerGroup": "drain-test-cg",
          "acks": "all",
          "enableIdempotence": true
        }
      },
      "chaosSpec": {
        "experimentName": "node-maintenance",
        "disruptionType": "NODE_DRAIN",
        "targetNamespace": "kafka",
        "targetLabel": "strimzi.io/pool-name=brokers-gamma",
        "chaosDurationSec": 60,
        "delayBeforeSec": 0,
        "envOverrides": {
          "TARGET_NODE": "gamma"
        }
      },
      "steadyStateSec": 30,
      "maxRecoveryWaitSec": 180,
      "probes": [
        {
          "name": "isr-health-check",
          "type": "cmdProbe",
          "mode": "Continuous",
          "command": "kafka-topics.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --describe --under-replicated-partitions 2>/dev/null | grep -c 'Topic:' || echo '0'",
          "expectedOutput": "50",
          "comparator": "<=",
          "intervalSec": 10,
          "timeoutSec": 30
        },
        {
          "name": "partition-availability",
          "type": "cmdProbe",
          "mode": "Continuous",
          "command": "kafka-topics.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --describe --unavailable-partitions 2>/dev/null | grep -c 'Topic:' || echo '0'",
          "expectedOutput": "0",
          "comparator": "==",
          "intervalSec": 10,
          "timeoutSec": 30
        }
      ]
    },

    {
      "_name": "09 — Rolling Restart (ROLLING_RESTART)",
      "_description": "Restart all brokers one at a time through the Strimzi Cluster Operator, which waits for each broker to be ready before it restarts the next. Simulates a rolling upgrade or routine maintenance window.",
      "_hypothesis": "Strimzi's rolling update mechanism ensures controlled shutdown between broker restarts. Producers with acks=all experience <5s latency per restart. No data loss.",
      "testRequest": {
        "type": "LOAD",
        "spec": {
          "topic": "kates-metrics",
          "numRecords": 900000,
          "recordSize": 512,
          "throughput": 3000,
          "acks": "all",
          "enableIdempotence": true
        }
      },
      "chaosSpec": {
        "experimentName": "rolling-restart",
        "disruptionType": "ROLLING_RESTART",
        "targetNamespace": "kafka",
        "targetLabel": "strimzi.io/cluster=krafter,strimzi.io/broker-role=true",
        "chaosDurationSec": 180,
        "delayBeforeSec": 0
      },
      "steadyStateSec": 30,
      "maxRecoveryWaitSec": 120,
      "probes": [
        {
          "name": "isr-health-check",
          "type": "cmdProbe",
          "mode": "Continuous",
          "command": "kafka-topics.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --describe --under-replicated-partitions 2>/dev/null | grep -c 'Topic:' || echo '0'",
          "expectedOutput": "50",
          "comparator": "<=",
          "intervalSec": 10,
          "timeoutSec": 30
        },
        {
          "name": "cluster-ready",
          "type": "k8sProbe",
          "mode": "Edge",
          "command": "kafka Ready",
          "expectedOutput": "Ready",
          "comparator": "contains",
          "intervalSec": 15,
          "timeoutSec": 30
        }
      ]
    },

    {
      "_name": "10 — Full Game Day (Multi-Phase Scenario)",
      "_description": "Three sequential chaos steps with recovery windows: broker crash → CPU saturation → network partition. Two STEADY scenario phases take turns at 2000 rec/s: kates-events for the first 7 minutes, past this step's recovery window and the report it returns, then kates-results for the next 7. Models a realistic cascading incident.",
      "_hypothesis": "Cluster survives 3 sequential faults without producer errors. Each step's fault resolves before the next begins.",
      "_note": "Step 1 only — submit steps 2/3 as separate requests after step 1 ChaosResult=Pass",
      "testRequest": {
        "type": "LOAD",
        "scenario": {
          "name": "gameday-full",
          "baseSpec": {
            "topic": "kates-events",
            "numRecords": 1000000,
            "recordSize": 1024,
            "acks": "all",
            "enableIdempotence": true
          },
          "phases": [
            {
              "name": "events-load",
              "phaseType": "STEADY",
              "durationMs": 420000,
              "targetThroughput": 2000
            },
            {
              "name": "results-load",
              "phaseType": "STEADY",
              "durationMs": 420000,
              "targetThroughput": 2000,
              "spec": {
                "topic": "kates-results"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "chaosSpec": {
        "experimentName": "gameday-full",
        "disruptionType": "POD_DELETE",
        "targetNamespace": "kafka",
        "targetLabel": "strimzi.io/pool-name=brokers-alpha",
        "chaosDurationSec": 60,
        "delayBeforeSec": 30,
        "gracePeriodSec": 0
      },
      "steadyStateSec": 30,
      "maxRecoveryWaitSec": 180,
      "probes": [
        {
          "name": "isr-health-check",
          "type": "cmdProbe",
          "mode": "Continuous",
          "command": "kafka-topics.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --describe --under-replicated-partitions 2>/dev/null | grep -c 'Topic:' || echo '0'",
          "expectedOutput": "50",
          "comparator": "<=",
          "intervalSec": 10,
          "timeoutSec": 30
        },
        {
          "name": "cluster-ready",
          "type": "k8sProbe",
          "mode": "Edge",
          "command": "kafka Ready",
          "expectedOutput": "Ready",
          "comparator": "contains",
          "intervalSec": 15,
          "timeoutSec": 30
        },
        {
          "name": "min-isr-check",
          "type": "cmdProbe",
          "mode": "Edge",
          "command": "kafka-topics.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --describe --unavailable-partitions 2>/dev/null | grep -c 'Topic:' || echo '0'",
          "expectedOutput": "5",
          "comparator": "<=",
          "intervalSec": 15,
          "timeoutSec": 30
        }
      ]
    }
  ],

  "_usage": {
    "port_forward": "kates ports",
    "api_key": "export KATES_API_KEY=\"$(kubectl get secret kates-api-key -n kates -o jsonpath='{.data.api-key}' | base64 -d)\"",
    "submit_single": "jq '.examples[0]' kates/docs/tutorials/resilience.json | curl -sS -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/resilience -H \"X-API-Key: $KATES_API_KEY\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d @- | jq '{status, error, runId: .performanceReport.run.id, impactDeltas, recoveryTime}'",
    "get_report": "curl -sS -H \"X-API-Key: $KATES_API_KEY\" http://localhost:8080/api/tests/{runId}/report | jq",
    "list_scenarios": "curl -sS -H \"X-API-Key: $KATES_API_KEY\" http://localhost:8080/api/resilience/scenarios | jq",
    "notes": [
      "kates ports forwards the Kates API to http://localhost:8080. Every /api endpoint but /api/health needs the key, whose Secret is in kates-stack instead with the single-namespace topology.",
      "submit_single sends examples[0], example 01; change the index to send another. It answers with one JSON report once the probes pass after the fault, or maxRecoveryWaitSec runs out.",
      "get_report takes the runId submit_single prints. The test run goes on after that answer, and its report is final once the run is DONE."
    ],
    "script_alternatives": {
      "broker_delete": "./scripts/test-chaos-broker-delete.sh",
      "cpu_hog":       "./scripts/test-chaos-broker-cpu-hog.sh",
      "net_partition": "./scripts/test-chaos-network-partition.sh",
      "disk_io":       "./scripts/test-chaos-disk-io-stress.sh",
      "full_gameday":  "./scripts/test-chaos-gameday.sh"
    }
  }
}
